{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1086182-why-don-t-we-have-mention-of-wu-keng-born-without-penises","id":1086182,"title":"Why don't we have mention of Wu Keng born without Penises...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-01T07:17:46-07:00","id":1086182,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Why don't we have mention of Wu Keng born without Penises...","content":"One thing that really bothered me about the Wu Keng is they never at all address what about Mages that awaken in Female, as in genitals are female, bodies. They make it seem like that isn't even a thing, and only males are mages and their genders are coerced into something more suitable to be a Demon Kings Concubine.<br /> <br /> And what do you think about Wu Keng training sorcerers? Awakened are rare after all, one in a million actually, and its especially difficult to find young ones you can mold, but you can start molding Sleepers into your paradigm and teach them Sorcery, like Hermetics love doing.<br /> <br /> I bring this all up because an NPC I am going to have in my Werewolf the Wyld West Game is going to be a Kitsune as a Mirror of a Shintai, and she going to be someone raised in a Wu Keng Cult, who stole their sorcery and left after her first change. And I want to know my options. I plan to have her teach sorcery to her mortal group, her batsu, to serve as a sort of collective of witches which help analyze and convert stolen magics, sorcery paths.<br /> <br /> So I find it very suspect that the Wu Keng would throw away a resource like a mage just because she doesn't have a penis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T09:22:32-07:00","id":1086220,"title":"","content":"Hoo boy.<br /> <br /> When you're dealing with the juk ak, the coercion <i>is the point</i>, and infernalist Awakenings have always been a touch different, in part because it wasn't impossible for a powerful being to trigger an Awakening in the early days of the game. So it's less that the WK keep an eye out for Awakened (and, really, the model that people Awaken as blank slates and get recruited doesn't jibe with much of the setting material) to co-opt and more that they induct victims who are Awakened by infernal means.<br /> <br /> I'd suggest replacing the WK in particular with a homebrew Infernal cult. You'll hit all the same beats and won't have to deal with the fraught history of the Craft of &quot;evil scheming transvestites&quot;. While I think DotE did yeoman's work in rehabilitating the whole concept, it's a very deep hole and I can't see why anyone would want to dig themselves out of it if they could just...not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T13:55:11-07:00","id":1086322,"title":"","content":"It always sounded to me like the Wu Keng were either born within the sect already, or obtained very young, since they're raised &quot;as women&quot;. If that's the case, then between the Wu Keng's arts and their demonic masters, it may well be that they only have babies who would be assigned male at birth. If they're obtained or abducted, they likely would only take assigned-male-at-birth babies.<br /> <br /> Given that this particular sect is enslaved by demon masters, I don't think that it would be a matter of the Wu Keng &quot;throwing away&quot; a resource as it is them complying with the terms laid down by their Masters.<br /> <br /> But honestly, I second Five Eyes. The Wu Keng are interesting, but very problematic from the get go. As someone who doesn't have very much experience with trans issues, I would never trust myself to know how to deal with the Wu Keng appropriately. If you have that knowledge, then more power to you, but if not, then I'd recommend leaving them alone. It doesn't sound like your Kitsune's concept requires the Wu Keng specifically. You might be able to work with an infernalist or barabbus sect of Akashics or Wu Lung instead, if you don't want to create a group from scratch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}